{# THE MODULE GRID — every module switched on for this area, one card, one page.

   Design: areas/<area>/modules.html in the design workspace.

   THE PICTURE IS THE SHELL'S PARTIAL, included with `with_context: false`
   because it takes exactly one variable and reading anything else off this
   page's context would couple the two. The catalogue picture has to be the same
   picture wherever it appears — this tab, a department page, a search result —
   and the way to guarantee that is to have one copy of it.

   THE TILES CARRY NO HEADLINE FIGURE, and that is a MISSING CONTRIBUTION CONTRACT rather than a
   missing style. The design draws a statistic, a sparkline and a one-line
   summary on every tile ("3,214 ha lost · 01–23"). Every one of those is a
   module's own reading of its own data, and there is no contribution contract for
   them: the catalogue publishes a slug, a name, a category, a status and a data
   source, and that is all anybody can honestly print. Inventing the numbers
   would be this bundle deciding what a forest-loss module measures — the exact
   coupling src/Overview's contracts exist to prevent. When a module can contribute a
   tile figure the way it already contributes an overview widget, the tiles grow
   one and this template does not change: the shell's ModuleCard does.

   THE PLATE CARRIES NO WIDGET INDEX — the design file's plate numbers are the
   workspace's referencing system and not product. See
   tests/Unit/Template/NoWorkshopLabelsTest.php. #}
{% extends '@Shell/page.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Modules{% endblock %}

{% block stylesheets %}
    {{ parent() }}
    {{ include('@Area/_stylesheets.html.twig') }}
{% endblock %}

{% block shell_breadcrumbs %}
    <a href="{{ path('area_index') }}">uhifadhi</a> /
    <a href="{{ path('area_index') }}">areas</a> /
    <a href="{{ path('area_show', {uuid: area.uuidString}) }}">{{ area.name|lower }}</a> / modules
{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_title %}{{ area.name }} &mdash; Modules{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_subtitle %}Every module switched on for this area &mdash; one card, one page. Open a card to view it; edit or run its data from there.{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_actions %}
    {# THE AFFORDANCE CARRIES THE PERMISSION. Composing an area is
       `modules.configure` — see AreaModulesController for why that pair and not
       a role. #}
    {% if door('modules.configure') %}
        <a class="cta" href="{{ path('area_modules_configure', {uuid: area.uuidString}) }}">{{ ux_icon('shell:sliders-horizontal') }} Modules</a>
    {% endif %}
{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page %}
    {{ include('@Shell/_module_grid.html.twig', {groups: groups}, with_context: false) }}

    {% if door('modules.configure') %}
        {# THE HONEST ADD AFFORDANCE — the shop, not a dead plus, and it says how
           many modules are actually waiting in it rather than implying there is
           always something to add. #}
        <div class="grid g4">
            <a class="c mtile-add" href="{{ path('area_modules_configure', {uuid: area.uuidString}) }}">
                <span class="t">{{ ux_icon('shell:plus') }} Add a module</span>
                <span class="d">
                    {%- if parkedCount > 0 -%}
                        {{ parkedCount }} in the catalogue {{ parkedCount == 1 ? 'is' : 'are' }} parked on this area.
                    {%- else -%}
                        Every module in the catalogue is switched on here.
                    {%- endif -%}
                </span>
            </a>
        </div>
    {% endif %}
{% endblock %}
